        "genres": "Real Time Strategy (RTS)|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "21",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/pikmin-2",
        "cached_at": 1772208565
      },
      {
        "id": 4036,
        "name": "NBA Street Vol. 2",
        "summary": "NBA Street Vol. 2 is a basketball video game, published by EA Sports BIG and developed by EA Canada. It is the sequel to NBA Street and the second game in the NBA Street series. It was released on April 28, 2003 for the PlayStation 2, GameCube, and, for the first time in the series, on the Xbox. Japan was only able to see a PlayStation 2 release of this game. The GameCube version was also planned to be released in that region, but it was canceled for unknown reasons.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2etl.jpg",
        "release_date": 1051488000,
        "rating": 87.5674061435354,
        "rating_count": 42,
        "genres": "Sport|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "11,21,8",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/nba-street-vol-2",
        "cached_at": 1772208565
      },
      {
        "id": 974,
        "name": "Resident Evil 4",
        "summary": "Resident Evil 4 is the sixth installment in the Resident Evil series and is often noted for its departure from the fixed camera angles of earlier titles. It introduced an over-the-shoulder third-person perspective, faster-paced gunplay, and more dynamic controls. The game features larger, more open environments and a new AI system that enables enemies to coordinate attacks and attempt to corner the player. Enemies exhibit more human-like behavior, such as climbing ladders, opening doors, and using weapons.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2wk8.jpg",
        "release_date": 1105401600,
        "rating": 87.44215112910966,
        "rating_count": 1590,
        "genres": "Shooter|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "21",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/resident-evil-4",
        "cached_at": 1772208565
      },
      {
        "id": 1033,
        "name": "The Legend of Zelda: The Wind Waker",
        "summary": "The Legend of Zelda: The Wind Waker is the first Zelda game for the Nintendo GameCube and also the first in the series to employ cel-shading, a lighting and texturing technique that results in the game having a cartoon-like appearance. Like its predecessors, The Wind Waker is an action game with puzzle-solving and light role-playing elements. Basic gameplay mechanics are similar to those found in Ocarina of Time, but it differentiates itself with its massive Great Sea which must be explored using a boat named King of Red Lions.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co3ohz.jpg",
        "release_date": 1039737600,
        "rating": 87.19146835527651,
        "rating_count": 999,
        "genres": "Puzzle|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "21",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/the-legend-of-zelda-the-wind-waker",
        "cached_at": 1772208565
      },
      {
        "id": 4041,
        "name": "NFL Street",
        "summary": "NFL Street is a series of sports video games developed by EA Tiburon and published by Electronic Arts. It combines the talent and big names of the NFL with the atmosphere of street football",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2ekg.jpg",
